---
source: crates/vitrify-cli/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: "long_help(&cmd, &path)"
---
Record a change entry's bookkeeping: journal events, Stale marks or re-recorded traces, the ledger

Usage: vitrify change <COMMAND>

Commands:
  apply  Apply the last change entry of each Active SDD: the `change` event, then Stale marks (MINOR, MAJOR) or re-recorded traces (PATCH), then the ledger (working tree only)
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Subcommands: apply (a change entry's bookkeeping in one step: re-stamp or mark Stale, the
         journal, the ledger)
Exit status: 2 without a subcommand; see each subcommand's --help
Examples:
  vitrify change apply --sdd specs/calc
  vitrify change apply --all --dry-run
